[["heading","F U L L - S TA C K  S O F T WA R E  E N G I N E E R I N G  I N T E R V I E W  /  3 2\nPractical Coding\nExercises"],["text","Complete Visual Teaching Edition"],["sinhala","","සිංහල + English | Java • JavaScript • SQL • React • REST • Git",321],["heading","40"],["heading","Worked exercises\n23 + 17"],["heading","Original + additional\n80"],["text","Local test assertions passed"],["heading","Core interview workflow"],["text","INPUT\nClarify requirements\nChoose examples"],["text","STEP 1\nBrute force\nBetter approach"],["text","STEP 2\nWrite code\nDry run\nTest"],["text","RESULT\nExplain time + space"],["heading","Golden rule"],["text","First solve a tiny example by hand. Then write readable code, test edge cases, and explain\ncomplexity. Never memorize a solution without understanding the invariant."],["sinhala","","මුලින් example එක අතින් solve කරන්න. ඊට පස්Jස් code එක ලියලා edge cases test කර time සහ space complexity පැහැදිලි කරන්න.",474],["text","Java methods are designed to be placed in a class; import java.util.* and java.math.BigInteger. JS examples use\nmodern JavaScript. Framework exercises use illustrative fragments where noted. Test results cover selected\ncases, not exhaustive correctness or production security."]]